dialect protocol
protocol stdio.gif.89a.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.gif.89a
start header

# Real GIF89a §17-27 file structure, matching this artifact's real `encode_gif`/`decode_gif`
# (../../⚙️engine/🦀️.rs) field-for-field: 6-byte ASCII magic "GIF89a", then the
# Logical Screen Descriptor (width/height u16LE x2, one packed flags byte incl. GCT-present/
# color-resolution/sort/GCT-size, bg color index, pixel aspect ratio) — ALL real, individually
# walked fields, exactly matching PNG's own IHDR treatment (P2-M2's own worked PNG example)
# and 87a's own sibling protocol file.
#
# This is the SEMIO-envelope-UNWRAPPED payload (P2-M3 §3/§5 point 4) — `GifSnapshot::
# encode_pack_with` (../../🦀️.rs) is `encode_gif(self)` wrapped by `store::
# semio_format::wrap_binary`, so the bytes this file walks start exactly where the envelope's
# own 8-byte magic + u32le token-length + token hand off (described once, framework-side, at
# 🧰️framework/…/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️.protocol.semio) — NOT re-described here.
#
# P2-FG2 NEW mechanism-gap, confirmed live (not assumed) by a real `walk_protocol` run
# against 87a's own sibling protocol file: `framing magic` unconditionally reads EXACTLY 8
# bytes for its byte-check, regardless of how many hex digits the declared literal has — GIF's
# own real magic is only 6 bytes, shorter than every existing real `framing magic` precedent
# in this repo (PNG's 8-byte signature, the framework's own SEMIO-envelope magic, the `.spk`
# container magic, all coincidentally exactly 8 bytes). Recorded as
# `protocol-framing-magic-fixed-8-bytes` (not yet in the recipe's §5 table; see 87a's own
# sibling protocol file for the full worked failure). Modeled honestly: `framing record` (no
# magic byte-check) + a real, individually-read `field magic fixed 6` — genuinely walked but
# not byte-validated at the PROTOCOL layer (the real Rust `decode_gif` already validates it
# byte-for-byte, `data[0..6] != b"GIF89a"`).
framing record

header fixed 13
field magic fixed 6
field width u16
field height u16
field packed u8
field bg_color_index u8
field pixel_aspect_ratio u8

# Past the fixed 13-byte magic + Logical Screen Descriptor, the real remaining bytes are: an OPTIONAL
# Global Color Table (`3 * 2^((packed & 0x07) + 1)` bytes, present iff `packed & 0x80 != 0`),
# then a repeated, TWO-LEVEL tag-dispatched block sequence (0x21 Extension Introducer, then a
# label byte: 0xF9 Graphic Control Extension / 0xFF Application Extension / 0xFE Comment
# Extension / 0x01 Plain Text Extension; 0x2C Image Descriptor + optional Local Color Table +
# a LZW-compressed sub-block chain; terminated by the 0x3B trailer byte) — a genuine, real
# NESTED `repeat` shape (§2.3's `nested <name> <prim> { arm ... }` GIF89a-cited construct),
# PLUS the ticket's own documented cross-block state carry (a decoded GCE's fields are
# consumed by the NEXT, different block).
#
# This artifact CANNOT express that `repeat` here, for the SAME two independent, genuine
# dialect reasons 87a's own sibling protocol file documents (neither is a PNG-style
# single-arm gap — both block the ENTIRE remainder, not one arm):
#   (a) `packed`'s GCT-presence bit IS testable (`Cond`'s `ge`/`eq` against the whole `packed`
#       byte value can gate presence), but the GCT's own BYTE LENGTH is `3 * 2^(size+1)` where
#       `size` is `packed`'s low 3 BITS — this dialect has no bitfield/sub-byte field
#       decomposition primitive at all (confirmed by reading `Prim`/`Cond`'s full grammar,
#       §2.2/§2.3 of the recipe) and no arithmetic-expression `Array` count source (`Count`
#       binds only to a literal `Fixed(n)`, `Varint`, or a named `Field`, never `field * k`).
#   (b) Since the GCT's own length can never be computed, the repeated block sequence's own
#       START position is unknowable declaratively — `repeat`'s own tag-dispatch (§2.3) needs
#       a known starting offset, which nothing past `packed` can supply.
# On TOP of (a)/(b), 89a additionally hits the census's own documented
# `gif/89a` row gap: cross-block state carry (a GCE's decoded fields consumed by a LATER,
# different block) — beyond ANY per-block-local field env `walk_fields` provides, even before
# (a)/(b) are considered. Recorded as a NEW mechanism-gap (not yet in the recipe's §5
# consolidated table): `protocol-bitfield-bytelen-computation` (shared with 87a) plus the
# census's own already-named cross-block-state-carry gap. The Rust `encode_gif`/`decode_gif`
# side IS genuinely, fully structured (real bit-shift GCT-size decode, real two-level
# tag-dispatched block loop, real `pending_gce` cross-block carry, real LZW sub-block chain) —
# this is purely a limit on how deep the PROTOCOL DESCRIPTION can validate structurally past
# the fixed screen descriptor, same documented-limitation shape as PNG's own
# `protocol-repeat-length-not-named`/DWG's encrypted-segment carve-out (§6).
chain rest bytes
